		{
			"id": "ePPyb3rkLMNLYLZOq",
			"description": "Meltagun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Imperium's dedicated close-range anti-armour infantry weapon, flash-vaporising the target's outer surface with a superheated fusion reaction; fiction across every era treats it as able to gut a tank at point-blank range and as nearly worthless at any distance, in sharp contrast to a lascannon's much longer reach.\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed melta anchor: 8dx6(10) burn at ½D, \"much less beyond\" 4dx6(3). Checked against the vehicle armour table with the exact dice distribution: AV14 (DR 350, a Leman Russ or Land Raider's front) has effective DR 35 against the (10) armour divisor; 8dx6 averages 168, always penetrating, so it easily beats even the heaviest armour in the framework's table at ½D range, as the assignment requires - the same holds at every lower AV on the table. The sharp drop-off is modelled as a second weapon line rather than a formula: beyond ½D the round keeps only half its dice (4d instead of 8d, the usual GURPS halving for range) but keeps a x6 multiplier and a much weaker (3) armour divisor instead of (10), representing the fusion reaction losing coherence and cohesion in open air before it reaches the target. Checked against the AV table: beyond ½D it averages 84 and still wrecks AV12 (DR 200, effective DR 66) 76% of the time and AV10-11 (DR 100/150) 94-100% of the time, but drops to 34% against AV13 (DR 275) and just 5% against AV14 (DR 350) - \"almost never beats\" the heaviest tanks, exactly as the framework specifies. ST 10 and a very short 10/50 range band (versus a boltgun's 200/1000) capture the weapon's role as a close-assault specialist, not a rifle.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
